Task 4.2: Add outbox-CDC example (same-transaction write + rollback demo)

Summary: OutboxExampleSuite.scala demonstrates writing a $domain_name$ row
and an outbox_events row in one Skunk session.transaction.use block, against
a self-contained session (not the real $domain_name;format="cap"$Store),
mirroring order-service's OrderStore.insertOutboxRow pattern. Two tests: (1)
the happy path - both rows exist after one successful transaction; (2) a
rollback proof - reusing the same outbox id across two transactions violates
outbox_events' primary key, failing the second transaction entirely, and the
second entity's row is confirmed absent (count 0) - proving the two writes
really are atomic together, not just two inserts that happened to both
succeed in the common case.

